<header class="chrome">
  <div class="title-bar">
    <span class="traffic"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
    <span class="title-id">webcloner://capture</span>
    <span class="title-status">SESSION_OK</span>
  </div>
  <div class="menu-bar">
    <a class="menu-item" href="#capture">01&nbsp;CAPTURE</a>
    <a class="menu-item" href="#features">02&nbsp;FEATURES</a>
    <a class="menu-item" href="#workflow">03&nbsp;WORKFLOW</a>
    <span class="menu-spacer"></span>
    <a class="menu-cta" href="#capture">START_CAPTURE&nbsp;↗</a>
  </div>
</header>

<header class="sr-only" aria-live="polite">
  <div aria-busy="true" id="progress" hidden aria-label="Downloading" role="progressbar"></div>
</header>

<main role="main">
  <section class="hero" id="capture" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> &gt; boot webcloner --simplified</p>
        <h1>Turn a website into a <em>portable</em> project<span class="caret" aria-hidden="true">▍</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Capture the source code and accessible assets from a website you own or are authorized to reproduce. Download a clean, bound archive and get back to work.</p>
        <ol class="hero-proof" aria-label="Product highlights">
          <li><strong>01</strong>&nbsp; Paste a URL</li>
          <li><strong>02</strong>&nbsp; Capture assets</li>
          <li><strong>03</strong>&nbsp; Download ZIP</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="console rack">
        <div class="console-body">
          <p class="prompt-status">$ webcloner capture --target=<span class="target-demo">https://your-website.com</span></p>
          <div class="card-topline">
            <span class="live-indicator"><span></span> Ready to capture</span>
            <span class="card-kicker">NEW_PROJECT</span>
            <div class="capture-intent">
              <span class="intent-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span>
              <span><strong>AUTHORIZED_SOURCE</strong><small>private workflow &middot; no account</small></span>
              <span class="intent-badge">[ZIP]</span>
              <span class="intent-badge adaptive">[ADAPT]</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <form class="download-form" id="downloadForm">
            <label class="sr-only" for="website">Website address</label>
            <div class="input-wrap">
              <span class="input-icon" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
              <input class="website-input" type="text" id="website" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" placeholder="https://your-website.com" aria-describedby="download-help" required />
            </div>
            <button class="download-button" id="download" type="submit"><span>Run capture</span><span class="button-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
          </form>
          <p class="sr-only" id="download-help">Enter a website address such as example.com or https://example.com.</p>

          <div class="capture-meta">
            <span><span class="checkmark">✓</span> No account required</span>
            <span><span class="checkmark">✓</span> ZIP export</span>
            <span><span class="checkmark">✓</span> Live progress</span>
            <span><span class="checkmark">✓</span> Adaptive engine</span>
          </div>

          <section class="progress-panel" id="downloadProgress" hidden aria-labelledby="progress-title">
            <div class="progress-summary">
              <div><strong id="progress-title">CAPTURE_STATUS</strong><p id="progressSummary">Waiting for a capture to begin.</p></div>
              <span class="download-count" id="nFilesP">FILES: <span id="nFiles">0</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="capture-progress-grid">
              <div class="progress-orbit" id="progressRing" data-state="idle" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="orbit-core"><span id="progressPhase">Idle</span><strong id="progressPercent">0%</strong></div>
              </div>
              <ol class="progress-steps" aria-label="Capture stages">
                <li class="progress-step" id="progressStep1" data-state="idle"><span class="step-dot">01</span><span><strong>Discover</strong><small>reading page structure</small></span></li>
                <li class="progress-step" id="progressStep2" data-state="idle"><span class="step-dot">02</span><span><strong>Collect</strong><small>fetching accessible files</small></span></li>
                <li class="progress-step" id="progressStep3" data-state="idle"><span class="step-dot">03</span><span><strong>Package</strong><small>building your zip</small></span></li>
                <li class="progress-step" id="progressStep4" data-state="idle"><span class="step-dot">04</span><span><strong>Ready</strong><small>archive complete</small></span></li>
              </ol>
            </div>
            <div class="site-preview-panel" id="sitePreviewPanel" hidden>
              <div class="site-preview-head"><span><span class="preview-live-dot"></span> SOURCE_PREVIEW</span><span id="sitePreviewStatus">Preparing</span></div>
              <div class="site-preview-frame">
                <div class="site-preview-skeleton" id="sitePreviewSkeleton" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><div></div></div>
                <img class="site-preview-image" id="sitePreviewImage" alt="Preview of the website being captured" hidden />
                <div class="site-preview-fallback" id="sitePreviewFallback" hidden><span id="sitePreviewInitial">W</span><strong id="sitePreviewDomain">Preparing preview</strong><small>This site does not allow a visual thumbnail. Capture progress is still running.</small></div>
              </div>
              <p class="site-preview-caption" id="sitePreviewCaption">A visual reference will appear while the archive is being set.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="progress-track"><span></span></div>
            <p class="progress-status" id="downloadStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to capture.</p>
            <details class="raw-log"><summary>view_technical_log &gt;&gt;</summary><pre class="log" id="log" aria-label="Download log"></pre></details>
          </section>

          <div class="download-dock" aria-live="polite">
            <div class="download-dock-head"><div><span class="dock-eyebrow">── ARCHIVE_HANDOFF ──</span><strong id="downloadDockTitle">Download not started yet</strong></div><span class="dock-state waiting" id="downloadDockState">Waiting</span></div>
            <a class="result-button download-waiting" id="downloadResult" href="" download data-ready="false" aria-disabled="true" aria-describedby="downloadDockHint"><span id="downloadResultLabel">Download website assets</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            <button class="download-help-toggle" id="downloadHelpToggle" type="button"><span class="help-button-icon" aria-hidden="true">?</span><span class="help-button-copy"><strong>Download not starting?</strong><small>open direct-download help</small></span><span class="help-button-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
            <p class="download-dock-hint" id="downloadDockHint">This button activates a direct ZIP download when your archive is ready.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="download-modal" id="downloadModal" hidden>
            <div class="download-modal-backdrop" data-close-download-modal></div>
            <div class="download-modal-card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="downloadModalTitle" aria-describedby="downloadModalCopy">
              <button class="modal-close" id="downloadModalClose" type="button" aria-label="Close download help">×</button>
              <span class="modal-icon" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <p class="eyebrow">DOWNLOAD_HANDOFF</p>
              <h3 id="downloadModalTitle">Your archive is still being prepared</h3>
              <p id="downloadModalCopy">Keep this tab open while WebCloner finishes collecting and packaging the accessible files. The direct download will activate here when it is ready.</p>
              <div class="modal-actions"><button class="modal-secondary" id="downloadModalDismiss" type="button">Keep waiting</button><a class="modal-direct" id="downloadModalDirect" href="" download hidden>Try direct download <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="permission-note"><span aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span> Only capture websites and content you own or have permission to reproduce.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stats-strip" aria-label="Capture capabilities">
    <div class="stats-inner">
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat-prefix">#1</span><span><strong>Full source capture</strong><small>HTML, CSS, JS and assets</small></span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat-prefix">#2</span><span><strong>Fast, focused workflow</strong><small>Paste, capture, download</small></span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat-prefix">#3</span><span><strong>Built for real work</strong><small>Backup, migration, development</small></span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">SECTION 01 &middot; CAPACITIES</p>
      <h2 id="features-title">A better starting point for your next build.</h2>
      <p>Whether you are moving a client site, preserving a project, or studying a layout, WebCloner keeps the first step simple.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-ledger">
      <article class="feature-row">
        <span class="feature-tag coral">&gt; 01</span>
        <div><h3>Bring the whole front end with you.</h3><p>Collect the accessible files that make a site work — from page structure and styles to scripts, images, and linked resources.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-row">
        <span class="feature-tag cyan">&gt; 02</span>
        <div><h3>Make a local copy you can work with.</h3><p>Use the exported files for authorized development, testing, audits, and handoffs without repeatedly loading the live site.</p><a class="text-link" href="#workflow">see_workflow <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-row">
        <span class="feature-tag amber">&gt; 03</span>
        <div><h3>Leave with a clean ZIP archive.</h3><p>Download a portable snapshot that is easy to store, share with your team, or open in your local development environment.</p><a class="text-link" href="#capture">start_capture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="plates" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="workflow-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">SECTION 02 &middot; PROCEDURE</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-title">From live URL to local workspace in three steps.</h2>
      <p>Skip the scattered downloads and manual asset hunting. WebCloner gives you a clear capture flow with progress you can actually follow.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps-list">
      <li><span class="step-number">%01</span><span><strong>Enter an authorized URL</strong><small>Paste the website address you own or have permission to reproduce.</small></span></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">%02</span><span><strong>Capture accessible resources</strong><small>WebCloner downloads the source and linked assets it can reach.</small></span></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">%03</span><span><strong>Download your archive</strong><small>Open the ZIP locally and continue with your migration or build.</small></span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="safety-card" id="safety" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
    <div class="safety-symbol" aria-hidden="true">+ OK</div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">SECTION 03 &middot; POLICY</p><h2 id="safety-title">Your authorization matters.</h2><p>WebCloner is intended for websites and content you own or are authorized to reproduce. It does not bypass logins, paywalls, or access controls, and technical access does not grant ownership of third-party content.</p></div>
  </section>
</main>

